; FILED: `(with-region (quote name))` — the ONE with-region spelling on which
; native and the VM disagree, and the only divergence this form has left.
;
; The reader is the whole story. The native tokenizer sees TOKEN_QUOTE for the
; sugar `'name` and keeps that fact, so the native front end can tell the
; SPECIFIER `'name` apart from a body expression that happens to be the list
; `(quote name)`. The VM reader (vm_parser.c) lowers both spellings to the same
; two-element list `(quote name)` and cannot distinguish them, so
; compile_form_with_region() reads the sole argument as a specifier and the form
; as having an EMPTY body.
;
; native -r : foo   — the body expression `(quote name)` evaluates to the symbol
; vm        : ()    — "specifier, empty body"; the empty-body branch reports
;                     `ERROR: with-region requires at least one body expression`
;                     on stderr and pushes OP_NIL so the caller's balancing
;                     OP_POP has a value to discard.
;
; DEGENERATE BY CONSTRUCTION, which is why the trade is taken rather than fixed:
; a with-region whose entire body is a quoted symbol allocates nothing, so the
; region does no work and the form is equivalent to the quote alone. Fixing it
; would require the VM reader to carry the sugar-vs-explicit distinction the
; native tokenizer has — a reader change of far wider blast radius than the
; degenerate form is worth.
;
; NOT A REGRESSION OF THE GATED SURFACE: all three DOCUMENTED spellings
; (anonymous, `'name`, `('name size)`) are value-identical on both substrates
; and gated by corpus/with_region_lowering.esk.  Before that corpus row the VM
; mis-lowered the form outright (stranded operands shifted later top-level
; slots; `('name size)` compiled as a call).
;
; PARITY NOTE FOR FUTURE CORPUS AUTHORS: the VM emits a literal `ERROR:` token
; on stderr for this spelling, and vm_stderr_clean() in scripts/run_vm_parity.sh
; treats that token as a failed run.  A corpus/ or oos/ file that uses
; `(with-region (quote name))` will therefore red the gate — use the sugar
; `'name` spelling, which is gated and agrees.
;
; Documented in-code at lib/backend/vm_compiler.c::compile_form_with_region.
(display (with-region (quote foo)))
(newline)
